path ui-canvas
kind layer
author ai
group render
note The boundary between the element tree and the GPU. A frame's picture leaves the ui crate as a DrawList: a flat, ordered vector of Commands in window pixels - set the clip, fill a rectangle, fill a quad, a circle, a run of text, a grid of coloured cells - with no element, no id and no wgpu type in it. Everything that draws (the tree's own painting, the graph's custom closure) writes through a Canvas, which keeps the clip stack and turns lines and curves into quads, so the platform's Renderer only replays primitives and never clips, measures or tessellates anything on its own. The one thing the ui side needs back from the font is the cell and row size at a pixel size; that is the Measure trait, which the Renderer implements and a test implements with a fixed cell. So the ui crate lays out and draws with no GPU, and the platform crate draws with no knowledge of elements: the DrawList is the whole contract, and a test can compare it command by command.

